{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"216fe19cd2834b7bb4dcc34b37fa33c9968b47825d9bc71eff8057b06174977f","digest":{"component_or_area":"mutation differ / snapshot reconciler","key_entities":["compute_mutations","field_drift","unbound_local","_compute_mutations_emit_both","test_key_set_prev_field_drift_never_survives_the_production_filter","test_a_genuinely_new_remote_key_still_plans_its_inbound_create","test_seed_mutations_survive_the_suppression","mutation_count","Gerrit 1256","commit 6cdd4b00d9ee","prev_snapshot","curr_snapshot"],"problem_keywords":["differ contract","field drift","call-site suppression","production filter","local state","remote state","snapshot mutation"],"propositions":["The raw compute_mutations API correctly emits field_drift updates when given mismatched local and remote state, serving as a load-bearing positive control for callers.","The production snapshot call-site passes both prev_snapshot and curr_snapshot as remote Jira state, violating the raw API contract, requiring A4-1's call-site filter to suppress field_drift and unbound_local emissions.","The A4-1 call-site filter must remain in place to allow future migration to real local state without weakening the raw differ's pure contract.","The call-site filter correctly preserves genuine inbound-create and invariant-seed mutations while suppressing only the spurious field-drift emissions from mismatched remote state.","A converged reconciliation pass with the filter in place records mutation_count == 0 without spurious updates."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787555919424284001,"uuid":"8c5a0d9c-054f-4ab8-b9de-3b16f743540d"}